# SEO & AI/LLM Visibility Best Practices

## Next.js Metadata API (use instead of manual tags)

- **Always use `export const metadata: Metadata`** for SEO tags
- **Never use manual `<meta>` tags** in `<head>` for standard metadata
- Use `metadata.other` for custom meta tags (geo, PWA, social)
- Use `metadata.appleWebApp` for PWA Apple tags
- Use `metadata.icons` for favicons and apple-touch-icon
- Use `metadata.verification` for Google/Bing verification codes

## Required Files for Full Visibility

| File | Location | Purpose |
|------|----------|---------|
| `sitemap.ts` | `app/` | Dynamic sitemap for crawlers |
| `robots.ts` | `app/` | Crawler permissions + AI bots |
| `manifest.ts` | `app/` | PWA manifest |
| `feed.xml/route.ts` | `app/` | RSS feed for syndication |
| `llms.txt` | `public/` | AI/LLM readable summary |
| `llms-full.txt` | `public/` | Detailed AI context |
| `humans.txt` | `public/` | Site credits |
| `security.txt` | `public/.well-known/` | Security contact |

## AI Crawler Rules (in robots.ts)

Include rules for: `GPTBot`, `ClaudeBot`, `Google-Extended`, `PerplexityBot`, `CCBot`, `cohere-ai`

## Google Analytics (Next.js way)

import { GoogleAnalytics } from "@next/third-parties/google";
// Place AFTER </body> but inside </html>
<GoogleAnalytics gaId="G-XXXXXX" />## Scripts (Next.js way)

import Script from "next/script";
<Script id="my-script" strategy="afterInteractive">{`...`}</Script>## Structured Data

- Use JSON-LD in a component with `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`
- Include: `Person`, `Organization`, `WebSite`, `FAQPage`, `Article`

## What stays in `<head>`

Only these need manual `<head>` tags:
- `<link rel="preconnect">` (performance)
- `<link rel="dns-prefetch">` (performance)
- Dynamic oEmbed links
- Custom `rel="alternate"` links (llms.txt)